{
  "title": "F-01 | Native microscopy fluorescence analysis",
  "question": "How does recorded fluorescence change across the supplied cadmium-labelled microscopy acquisitions?",
  "materials": [
    "116 original supplied files and 4 derived context files; ND2, TIFF, AVI and experimental notes; original intensities preserved.",
    "nd2 0.12.0; tifffile 2026.10.15; scikit-image 0.26.0; SciPy 1.18.1."
  ],
  "methods": [
    "Stream native frames; distinguish T,C,P,Z axes; cross-check ND2 timestamps against per-frame metadata. Use acquired event Z coordinates and cross-check optical stacks against Z index and planned positions.",
    "Whole-field native means are primary. Estimate spatial background outside BF-derived regions; keep raw means and a 10th-percentile background sensitivity.",
    "BF high-pass regions use a fixed initial threshold, 1 \u00b5m expansion and 4\u2013150 \u00b5m\u00b2 area limits. Regions are not validated cells.",
    "Initial/final 10% medians; fractional changes only above 5\u00d7 spatial noise. Fixed-mask and 0.85/1.15 threshold sensitivity; every-frame clipping, focus and drift.",
    "Retain all frames. AVI is secondary export QC; old Z stacks and static fields are not time courses."
  ],
  "scope_and_assumptions": [
    "Conditions are nominal: 1 mM Cd stock contradicts the 5 mM labels. The C2 Ca 0/1 mM filename conflict is retained.",
    "Initial reference is recording-relative, not a verified pre-Cd baseline. TIFF clocks conflict; frame-index analysis only.",
    "Denoise.ai ON means acquisition-processed data, not unprocessed detector counts. BF-region masks do not establish single-cell identities; dense 30 September masks are incomplete.",
    "Native time-series exposure event values are missing and are not imputed from static-image 10 ms metadata. Stage Z varies, but focus compensation can move the objective; PFS state codes are opaque here. Pairs remain conditional on optical comparability. C1/Empty pairs change both Ca and Cd, so they do not isolate Cd.",
    "Fields/cells/frames/exports are not independent cultures. No automatic photobleach correction, culture p-values, binding or calibrated dose model."
  ],
  "results": [
    "120 input files, including derived context, were inventoried and byte-verified; 107 native/export image containers were processed.",
    "20 time-series acquisitions; 14 with native clocks. All 146 static/Z frames are retained; 141 contain fluorescence and 94 have a usable BF-region metric.",
    "13 October, nominal 10 mM Ca / 5 mM Cd: C8: +2.66 ADU over 298.2s; Empty: +0.12 ADU over 299.5s; C6: +15.01 ADU over 298.4s; C1: +0.57 ADU over 299.6s; C2: +0.77 ADU over 299.6s. The C6 recording has the largest within-recording increase in this group. Candidate field-matched pre/post contrasts are C1 -10.22 ADU; C2 +1.92 ADU; Empty +0.68 ADU. Within-recording change and the field-matched treatment contrast answer different questions: the C1 field decreases across its paired acquisitions despite rising slightly within the challenged recording.",
    "No recording met the preset resolved-plateau criterion; an empirical reaction time constant, t50 and t90 were not estimated.",
    "Four same-well comparisons meet the stage/BF field-match criterion. Their pre/post contrasts are tabulated separately from within-recording change.",
    "Recorded stage Z spans 2.34 \u00b5m in C2 Ca 1 mM / Cd 5 mM and 1.08 \u00b5m in C2 Ca 10 mM / Cd 5 mM. PFS Status is code 1 except for three code-5 frames across those two C2 recordings; PFS offsets are constant within all 14 native time series. Codes are retained without assigning a lock-state meaning; stage motion alone does not establish defocus.",
    "6 AVI files were decoded as processed-export QC and were not counted as additional biological observations."
  ],
  "conclusion": "13 October, nominal 10 mM Ca / 5 mM Cd: C8: +2.66 ADU over 298.2s; Empty: +0.12 ADU over 299.5s; C6: +15.01 ADU over 298.4s; C1: +0.57 ADU over 299.6s; C2: +0.77 ADU over 299.6s. The C6 recording has the largest within-recording increase in this group. Candidate field-matched pre/post contrasts are C1 -10.22 ADU; C2 +1.92 ADU; Empty +0.68 ADU. Within-recording change and the field-matched treatment contrast answer different questions: the C1 field decreases across its paired acquisitions despite rising slightly within the challenged recording.",
  "figures": [
    {
      "file": "01_inventory.png",
      "caption": "Input files and sequence frames or channel pairs. Native and exported files remain separately identified; bars are not biological replicate counts."
    },
    {
      "file": "02_native_traces.png",
      "caption": "All native time-series traces; references and positions belong to individual recordings. No Cd-addition frame is assumed."
    },
    {
      "file": "03_initial_reference.png",
      "caption": "Fractional changes use the first 10% of each recording, not a pre-exposure baseline. Ratios are omitted when the reference is too small relative to spatial background noise."
    },
    {
      "file": "04_change_sensitivity.png",
      "caption": "Acquisition-level whole-field changes with spatial background subtraction (bars) and untouched raw whole-field means (points). BF-region changes and fixed-mask sensitivity remain in the numerical tables."
    },
    {
      "file": "05_quality_diagnostics.png",
      "caption": "Every-frame translation, transmitted-light focus, mask coverage, clipping, recorded stage Z and spatial background. Stage motion alone does not establish defocus; recorded PFS codes/offsets accompany the Z trajectories in the QC tables. No automatic exclusion or bleaching correction was applied."
    },
    {
      "file": "06_segmentation.png",
      "caption": "Representative BF-only region masks. First, middle, last and at least 5% of frame overlays are supplied in quality_control/. Region counts are not certified cell counts."
    },
    {
      "file": "07_static_and_z.png",
      "caption": "Raw static-field means are separated by batch and optical settings. All B2/B10 fluorescence Z planes use acquired ND2 event coordinates and are retained, including out-of-focus planes without a usable BF-region mask; these are optical stacks, not biological time series."
    },
    {
      "file": "08_s1_control.png",
      "caption": "9 October S1 Cd-labelled and no-Cd exports. Clocks conflict within TIFF metadata, so the primary axis is frame index; each recording is normalized to its own initial reference."
    },
    {
      "file": "09_regions_and_thresholds.png",
      "caption": "Mask-threshold sensitivity and heterogeneity of sampled BF-defined regions. Object distributions are descriptive and do not supply biological replication."
    },
    {
      "file": "10_optical_and_clock_sensitivity.png",
      "caption": "Z-dependent focus is an optical diagnostic. TIFF time reconstruction assumes three-position interleaving; uniform header and reconstructed clock metrics are both tabulated, while primary TIFF results remain frame-index based."
    },
    {
      "file": "11_candidate_matched_fields.png",
      "caption": "Candidate same-field comparisons pass stage-distance and registered BF-correlation checks. Post values use initial/final 10% medians; the C2 calcium-conflict static file has a single post frame. C1/Empty comparisons change both calcium and cadmium labels; C2 R026 keeps nominal calcium at 1 mM. Field matching does not establish same-cell identity, equal exposure or addition time."
    }
  ],
  "references": [
    "Chen et al. (2013), Ultrasensitive fluorescent proteins for imaging neuronal activity. https://doi.org/10.1038/nature12354",
    "Montero Llopis et al. (2021), Best practices and tools for reporting reproducible fluorescence microscopy methods. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-021-01156-w",
    "nd2 official documentation: https://talleylambert.com/nd2/",
    "scikit-image registration documentation: https://scikit-image.org/docs/stable/api/skimage.registration.html",
    "Nikon Perfect Focus System: near-infrared focus compensation maintains objective-to-coverslip position. https://www.microscope.healthcare.nikon.com/en_EU/resources/glossary/perfect-focus-system",
    "Supplied 13 October lab notebook, body.b0029 (condition table), b0037\u2013b0069 (prior qualitative observations).",
    "Biomni methods review supplied in F01_biomni_methods_review.json; no arbitrary drift cutoff adopted."
  ],
